Package: scf
Title: Tools for Analyzing the Survey of Consumer Finances
Version: 1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Joseph", "Cohen", 
           email = "joseph.cohen@qc.cuny.edu", 
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(affiliation = "Department of Sociology, CUNY Queens College"))
Author: Joseph N. Cohen, Department of Sociology, CUNY Queens College
Maintainer: Joseph N. Cohen <joseph.cohen@qc.cuny.edu>
Description: 
  This package provides a suite of functions to support analysis of the public-
  use microdata release of the U.S. Federal Reserve's 'Survey of Consumer
  Finances' (SCF). It wraps the SCF's multiply-imputed, replicate-weighted
  data into a custom object class ('scf_mi_survey') and supports the estimation
  of population-level statistics from that object, including univariate 
  and bivariate variable distributions, hypothesis testing, data visualization, 
  and basic regression modeling. The package is designed to make the SCF's 
  public-use microdata accessible to analysts who are familiar with general 
  statistical methods but have not yet specialized in the analysis of multiply-
  imputed or complex survey data. All functions emphasize transparency, 
  reproducibility, and pedagogical clarity to facilitate diagnostics, 
  exploration, and learning.
